{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern","level":2,"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_modify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if more than 100 changes are drained within a single debounce interval (the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loopThreshold"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter; 250 ms by default). It counts only dispatches that changed an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":", and it reports once per burst — the count starts over after a whole debounce interval with no drains. This usually means an effect or plugin dispatches an action on every state change, feeding the cycle it reacts to. A steady stream of edits, such as a slider drag, stays well under the threshold and is not reported."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Debounced Persistence","anchor":"Debounced-Persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drain restarts the flush’s debounce timer, so a burst of edits is written once. The timer is never pushed further than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxWait"},{"type":"text","text":" past the oldest pending change (four debounce intervals, and at least a second, by default), so continuous edits still reach storage while they continue. A retry of a failed flush keeps its own schedule; a new edit postpones it only when the flush it schedules is due first and carries the failed batch anyway."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Effect Threading","anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","abstract":[{"text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" class tree for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxObservable","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","role":"article","title":"Design Principles","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","kind":"article","title":"Security Posture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it."}]}}}